# Quality gates and workflow

Zero tolerance for red code. A change is complete only when every gate below is green.
"Fix it in the next commit" is not a workflow that exists in {{PROJECT_NAME}}.

## While editing (every file, every cycle)

1. Save the file.
2. Run scoped gates on the changed paths:

```bash
npx eslint <changed paths>
npx tsc --noEmit --pretty false
```

3. **Triage every error:**
   - **Trivial** (typo, missing import, simple narrowing) → fix immediately, same cycle.
   - **Complex or cross-cutting** → stop; surface a correction plan (what is wrong, why a
     one-liner is unsafe, proposed scope, affected files) before patching.
4. Never suppress to bypass triage: no `// @ts-ignore`, no `as any`, no non-null assertion
   on un-narrowed values, no ad-hoc `// eslint-disable`.

## End of work cycle (mandatory, all must pass)

```bash
npm run lint                       # zero errors, zero new warnings
npx tsc --noEmit --pretty false    # zero errors
npm test                           # full Jest suite green
npm run i18n-verify                # when locale files were touched
```

- A failing or newly skipped test introduced by the change is a **regression**, not a TODO.
- Design-system or token changes additionally run the scoped design-system gate
  (`design-system/03-quality-gates.mdc`).
- Storybook story changes: regenerate the story registry and verify web Storybook renders
  without console errors.

## After every commit

- The working tree at each commit passes all gates — no "WIP, broken" commits on shared
  branches. Use local squashing before pushing if needed.
- CI re-runs lint, typecheck, and tests on every push and PR. **CI is a backstop, never
  the first place errors are discovered.**

## Definition of done

A change is done when: gates are green, tests for new logic exist, docs are updated,
the authoring checklist (`development/10-authoring-checklist.mdc`) passes, and the
security-review triggers (`security/01-security-principles.mdc`) were evaluated.
